1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,624
This photograph shows a ship's final moments.

2
00:00:03,674 --> 00:00:07,700
In 1915, in Antarctica, the ice crushed the Endurance.

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:12,136
Twenty-eight men were left on the ice in the most desolate place on Earth.

4
00:00:12,186 --> 00:00:13,951
No one was looking for them.

5
00:00:14,001 --> 00:00:16,909
This is the story of Shackleton and the Endurance.

6
00:00:16,959 --> 00:00:20,908
This ship stayed frozen in the ice, unable to move, for ten months.

7
00:00:20,958 --> 00:00:26,562
In January 1915, in the Weddell Sea, the ice closed in around the Endurance from every side.

8
00:00:26,612 --> 00:00:29,538
Winter came, and the sun did not rise for weeks.

9
00:00:29,588 --> 00:00:33,031
In October, the pressure of the ice broke the ship's keel.

10
00:00:33,081 --> 00:00:37,028
On the twenty-first of November, the Endurance disappeared among the ice.

11
00:00:40,078 --> 00:00:43,934
This photographer destroyed four hundred of his photographs with his own hands.

12
00:00:43,984 --> 00:00:49,079
Frank Hurley went into the flooded cabin of the sinking ship and rescued his glass negatives.

13
00:00:49,129 --> 00:00:50,737
But glass was too heavy.

14
00:00:50,787 --> 00:00:54,840
Out of more than five hundred images, he could take only one hundred and twenty with him.

15
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:58,799
Most of the photographs in this video come from those one hundred and twenty.

16
00:00:58,849 --> 00:01:01,141
They lived on the ice for months.

17
00:01:01,191 --> 00:01:07,884
In April 1916, when the ice broke up, they climbed into three small boats and rowed for seven days.

18
00:01:07,934 --> 00:01:13,354
When they reached Elephant Island, they stood on solid ground for the first time in four hundred and ninety-seven days.

19
00:01:13,404 --> 00:01:15,669
But no one would ever find them there.

20
00:01:15,719 --> 00:01:19,576
A seven-metre boat, thirteen hundred kilometres of open sea.

21
00:01:19,626 --> 00:01:24,422
Shackleton and five of his men set out across the world's roughest sea to find help.

22
00:01:24,472 --> 00:01:28,294
In sixteen days they saw the sun only four times.

23
00:01:28,344 --> 00:01:32,201
And they reached South Georgia exactly as they had planned.

24
00:01:32,251 --> 00:01:35,986
No maps, thirty-six hours, without stopping.

25
00:01:36,036 --> 00:01:39,186
Because the whaling station was on the other side of the island.

26
00:01:39,236 --> 00:01:43,862
Shackleton and two companions crossed mountains no one had ever crossed before.

27
00:01:43,912 --> 00:01:48,750
When they reached the station, their clothes were in rags and their faces unrecognisable.

28
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:54,644
On Elephant Island, twenty-two men waited for four and a half months under two upturned boats.

29
00:01:54,694 --> 00:01:59,226
Shackleton set out by ship three times, and three times the ice blocked the way.

30
00:01:59,276 --> 00:02:02,642
On the thirtieth of August, on the fourth attempt, he reached the island.

31
00:02:02,692 --> 00:02:04,341
He counted the men on the shore.

32
00:02:04,391 --> 00:02:05,667
Every one of them was there.

33
00:02:05,717 --> 00:02:08,223
This ship stayed lost for one hundred and six years.

34
00:02:08,273 --> 00:02:13,383
When it was found in 2022, three thousand metres deep, its name could still be read.

35
00:02:13,433 --> 00:02:17,603
The Endurance was lost, but not one of the twenty-eight men died.

36
00:02:17,653 --> 00:02:21,346
If you had been in that boat, would you have gone with Shackleton?
